{"id":"2610.31574","authors":[{"_id":"6adacbeb55db1e682e582d34","name":"Sihan Yang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adacbeb55db1e682e582d35","name":"Jie Huang","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adacbeb55db1e682e582d36","name":"Hanxuan Li","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adacbeb55db1e682e582d37","name":"Yifan Guo","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adacbeb55db1e682e582d38","name":"Weigao Sun","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adacbeb55db1e682e582d39","name":"Yiran Zhong","hidden":false},{"_id":"6adacbeb55db1e682e582d3a","name":"Weiyang Liu","hidden":false}],"publishedAt":"2026-10-22T17:14:38.000Z","submittedOnDailyAt":"2026-10-23T00:00:00.000Z","title":"Rethinking Sequence Compression with Test-time Regression","submittedOnDailyBy":{"_id":"6674e95a88b91ec3dddf8132","avatarUrl":"/avatars/41209068bdc91f97528a5d0c972802f4.svg","isPro":false,"fullname":"Sihan Yang","user":"sihany","type":"user","name":"sihany"},"summary":"Sequence compression is a fundamental operation and a critical information bottleneck in efficient language and multimodal models, and yet prevailing approaches based on pooling or learned projections remain underperforming. We revisit sequence compression through the lens of test-time regression: input tokens define a regression problem whose fitted coefficients form the compressed representation. Importantly, the regression problem is learned end-to-end via backpropagation, while its coefficients are computed efficiently in closed form during the forward pass. This leads to TTR-Compressor, a general alternative to conventional pooling and projection-based compression. We evaluate TTR-Compressor as the compressor for block-wise sparse attention and the visual token merger for multimodal large language models. On block-wise sparse attention, TTR-Compressor improves RULER performance over attention-based compressors by a large margin. For visual token merging, it consistently outperforms the standard MLP merger and matches its performance with 55.6% fewer visual tokens. These results establish test-time regression as an effective primitive for sequence compression in efficient language and multimodal models.","upvotes":10,"discussionId":"6adacbeb55db1e682e582d3b","projectPage":"https://spherelab.ai/ttr-compressor/","githubRepo":"https://github.com/Sphere-AI-Lab/ttr-compressor","githubRepoAddedBy":"user","ai_summary":"Test-time regression provides a learnable, closed-form alternative to pooling for compressing sequences in efficient language and multimodal models.","ai_keywords":["test-time regression","sequence compression","block-wise sparse attention","visual token merger","multimodal large language models"],"ai_summary_model":"thinkingmachines/Inkling-Small","githubStars":5,"organization":{"_id":"6814c6bec8d4f013b0851a7f","name":"SphereLab","fullname":"CUHK SphereLab","avatar":"https://cdn-avatars.huggingface.co/v1/production/uploads/648905d1a15c43c791d4381f/3vQFn8UJLYbGZ04CADQsJ.png"},"linkedModels":[],"numTotalModels":0,"linkedDatasets":[],"numTotalDatasets":0,"linkedSpaces":[],"numTotalSpaces":0}